#: ../../source/docs/throttle-boost.rst:5
#: 16c7baac415c45018f24150d256f2f3c
msgid "Throttle Boost"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throttle-boost.rst:7
#: c9dde50ff5c24a2a88866c038e5e03bc
msgid "Even well tuned Multicopters can momentarily lose tight attitude control with sudden, large throttle changes. Dips and Rolls can occur on \"punch-outs\" or \"throttle chops\", especially on light vehicles with high thrust to weight ratios."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throttle-boost.rst:9
#: b8458ede51574675a94bfb9440ce3278
msgid "In order to reduce this effect, the :ref:`ATC_THR_G_BOOST<ATC_THR_G_BOOST>` parameter can be adjusted. Normally inactive at its default value of \"0\", setting this to a non-zero number will provide PID gain multiplication anytime the throttle is changed rapidly, either up or down. At the :ref:`ATC_THR_G_BOOST<ATC_THR_G_BOOST>` parameter's maximum value of one (1), the  rate PIDs will be increased by a factor of 2 and the Angle PIDs will be increased by a value of 4 during the time the throttle is being rapidly changed. Lower values will result in lower gain multiplication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/throttle-boost.rst:11
#: 7f55bcbb6b114ed0ab1c8ff5abb8b599
msgid "The less tightly tuned the vehicle is, the more it will require Throttle Boost."
msgstr ""
